OL,3,GNEWSAPolice seize customised bike
OL,4,A'capable of 28 mph'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA customised bicycle was seized by
OL,7,Fpolice in Nottinghamshire after they
OL,8,Fdiscovered it could reach speeds of
OL,9,Falmost 30mph (48 km/h).
OL,11,FOfficers from Kirkby in Ashfield
OL,12,Fstopped the vehicle on Tuesday and
OL,13,Ffound the bike had a scooter motor
OL,14,Froughly wired to a battery held on by
OL,15,Ftape. The rear wheel had also been
OL,16,Freplaced with a smaller solid wheel.
OL,18,FCurrent legislation states any bike
OL,19,Fpowered beyond 15.5mph (25 km/h) counts
OL,20,Fas a motor vehicle and requirements
OL,21,Fsuch as a driving licence and insurance
OL,22,Fcan apply.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
